------------------------------------------------------------------------------
jxl-rs
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This crate is a wrapper around jxl-rs (https://github.com/libjxl/jxl-rs, the
`jxl` crate), the JPEG XL project's own Rust decoder, which does the decoding
and is used under its BSD-3-Clause licence:

    Copyright (c) the JPEG XL Project Authors. All rights reserved.

The full licence text is in tests/data/LICENSE.jxl-rs. jxl-rs carries a
PATENTS file granting a royalty-free patent licence from Google for its JPEG
XL implementation (https://github.com/libjxl/jxl-rs/blob/main/PATENTS).

The test files in tests/data (*.jxl) are jxl-rs's test data, under the same
BSD-3-Clause licence.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The encoder (src/encode)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The encoder (lossless and lossy) is this crate's own code. The JPEG XL standard (ISO/IEC
18181) is not freely available, so the codestream's syntax it writes was
learned from jxl-rs's decoder source (above, BSD-3-Clause): what the decoder
reads, in what order, with what coding. No jxl-rs code is copied into it; its
output is checked by decoding it with jxl-rs. The format's constant tables
(the default dequantisation parameters, the AFV basis, the implicit
palette, the 2-D LZ77 distances, the static code-length codes) are the
format's own and appear in the encoder as data; jxl-rs's transform crate
(jxl_transforms, BSD-3-Clause) is used by the tests only, to check the
encoder's transforms. Google's PATENTS grant is for
its own JPEG XL implementations; this note makes no claim that it covers
this encoder.
